WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.393 --> 00:00:09.493
Sundarbans

00:00:09.493 --> 00:00:11.484
India's one and only place

00:00:11.484 --> 00:00:13.929
which has one of the most significant enviornmental

00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:15.929
and geographical values. 

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:20.643
It has the largest river delta

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:22.643
and mangrove forest on earth.

00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:27.357
Not only the nature,

00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:29.924
Sundarbans have the largest population of

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.080
Royal Bengal Tiger.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.528
But having all of these

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:38.528
still this place is quite unexplored

00:00:39.073 --> 00:00:41.073
by most of the people from India

00:00:41.351 --> 00:00:43.591
and also from many other countries

00:00:43.591 --> 00:00:44.497
around the World.

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:53.672
Recently, I got a chance to explore

00:00:53.672 --> 00:00:56.317
some of the parts of this National forest.

00:00:57.174 --> 00:00:58.718
And I was blown away,

00:00:58.718 --> 00:01:01.330
when I got into this place and realize,

00:01:01.753 --> 00:01:04.287
how we could ignore such a place

00:01:04.598 --> 00:01:06.598
which has breathtaking natural beauties

00:01:07.121 --> 00:01:10.133
and some of the most beautiful wild animals.

00:01:13.036 --> 00:01:15.036
During my visit, I realize

00:01:15.281 --> 00:01:17.281
that how we, as human beings,

00:01:18.149 --> 00:01:20.149
destroying our own life shield

00:01:20.772 --> 00:01:24.240
which is protecting us from various natural disasters.

00:01:24.919 --> 00:01:25.873
How we are ignoring

00:01:25.873 --> 00:01:28.730
the importance of this ecosystem.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.078
This is one of the reasons

00:01:31.078 --> 00:01:33.078
why these tigers are now endangered species.

00:01:35.492 --> 00:01:38.193
The forest land is also decreasing slowly

00:01:38.449 --> 00:01:40.449
due to the rise of Sea level

00:01:40.582 --> 00:01:43.439
which is a long term effect of Global warming

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:47.119
and we all are responsible for this.

00:01:53.816 --> 00:01:56.750
I know we can't change it over the night

00:01:56.872 --> 00:01:58.872
but we should think about it,

00:01:58.872 --> 00:02:00.872
we should protect our nature

00:02:00.872 --> 00:02:03.562
as it is protecting us from the beginning.

00:02:03.562 --> 00:02:10.766
[music]

00:02:47.916 --> 00:02:48.416
I wish,

00:02:48.983 --> 00:02:50.983
you'll also visit Sundarbans

00:02:51.328 --> 00:02:52.449
and witness

00:02:52.449 --> 00:02:54.649
our natural shield on your own.

00:02:55.027 --> 00:02:56.649
And then you'll realize

00:02:56.649 --> 00:02:58.649
the actual value of this place.

